<title>GERMANY: Zeitler says mark appreciation correction ended.</title>
<headline>Zeitler says mark appreciation correction ended.</headline>
<dateline>KRONACH, Germany 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said on Tuesday the mark's appreciation against other currencies has been completed and may have become somewhat excessive.</p>
<p>&quot;The appreciation of the deutschemark has been corrected in the meantime and that may even go somewhat beyond a correction,&quot; Zeitler told a regional business seminar in the German state of Bavaria.</p>
<p>Zeitler did not specify what exchange rates he was referring to in regard to the mark's movements.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
